From 0da8f4a84047fe99a240659ac111ecb8f41abf69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Alvarado Martinez <45523697+calvarado2004@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:43:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] helios: find native message boundaries with one tokenization

message_boundaries renders and tokenizes every message prefix of a request
to find its prefix-cache checkpoints. With the native DeepSeek encoders each
prefix render tokenizes the whole prefix, so a request costs messages x prompt
length on one frontend thread. A Qwen Code session at ~290K tokens kept the
frontend busy for more than 15 minutes before the request reached the
scheduler (GPU idle, 0 pending, 1 HTTP request in flight).

rendered_message_boundaries renders only the text of each prefix and cuts the
complete prompt where that text ends, through byte offsets from one encoding of
the prompt. It keeps a cut only at a token start. Jinja templates, and prompts
whose offset encoding does not reproduce their token IDs exactly, use
message_boundaries unchanged.

Tests compare the result with message_boundaries: agent sessions with tool
calls, dropped reasoning, Unicode and whitespace runs, image placeholders, the
fallback paths, and the checkpoint tokenizer (ignored without
FLARE_DEEPSEEK_TEST_SNAPSHOT). A 201K-token, 242-boundary session takes 1.2 s
instead of 26.1 s in a debug build.
